  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x?$\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$\n- $y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function.\n- $x=15\\pi $ is in the domain.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statements I and II are both false.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\u2026.$ Hence, statement III is false.",
